--- This file defines the sessions between a client and a TA: opening a session, invoking a command
--- in it, and closing it ([Internal Core] 2.1, 4.3, 4.5, 4.9, [Client API] 4.5.7-4.5.9).
---
--- A session is a Session object, sessionId(N), created by the TrustedOS when it opens the
--- session.  Its source is the client that opened it, an RA or a TA, and its destination the TA
--- instance that serves it; is-smc tells whether the source is an RA, reached through SMC, or a
--- TA, whose client identity is TEE_LOGIN_TRUSTED_APP ([Internal Core] 4.2.2, 4.6).  The two
--- kinds of client are one kind of session, see [Internal Core] 2.1: they differ only in the
--- channel of their requests and answers.
---
---                       RA client (TEEC_*)                  TA client (TEE_*TASession, ...)
---   open request        smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)   reqTrustedOS(openTASession(TN), TK)
---   open answer         smcRet(RI, (# success # SID))       retTrustedOS(openSessionSuccess(SID), TK)
---   invoke request      smcReq(RI, SID, FID, VL)            init(TeeInvokeTACommand[...]) of TK
---   to the TA instance  msg invkTa[FID VL] from SID to TI   msg invkTa[FID VL] from SID to TI
---   from the instance   msg invkTaRet[RET] from TI to SID   msg invkTaRet[RET] from TI to SID
---   invoke answer       smcRet(RI, (# success RET))         return(TeeInvokeTACommand[...]) of TK
---
--- VL are the argument values of the service, the values of the shared objects of the client, and
--- RET the results of the TA instance, the values of its output parameters (getVals).  The
--- session is the sender of the request to the instance, so the instance records the session in
--- its client-service, {SID, FID}, and answers it.
---
--- An RA holds the session as the value # SID; a TA holds a handle, a TaSessionHandle object
--- whose session attribute is SID.
---
--- The state of a session:
---   * idle: the session is open and no command is pending in it;
---   * invoking: a command of the source is pending, see [Internal Core] 2.1.3: there is at most
---     one in a session;
---   * targetDead: the destination has panicked while it served the pending command, see
---     [Internal Core] 2.3.3; a later command gets TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD at once.
---
--- Opening a session.  The TrustedOS decides in the same way for both kinds of client:
---   * the single-instance TA TN has no instance: the TrustedOS creates the instance from the
---     program of TN in ta-config, with the storage of TN, records it in ta-instances, and
---     opens the session on it;
---   * the instance of TN already has a session, and TN accepts one session at a time,
---     taConfig(P, true, false): TEE_ERROR_BUSY, TEEC_ERROR_BUSY for an RA;
---   * TN has an instance and accepts several sessions, taConfig(P, true, true): the session is
---     opened on that instance, which all the sessions of TN share, see [Internal Core] 2.1.6;
---   * TN is a multi-instance TA, taConfig(P, false, MS): the TrustedOS creates a new instance for
---     the session, see [Internal Core] 2.1.6, with the storage of TN; MS is ignored, see
---     [Internal Core] 4.5, as each instance has one session;
---   * no TA has the identifier TN: TEE_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND.
--- An instance counts its open sessions in sessions.  The storage of a TA is shared by all its
--- instances, see [Internal Core] 2.2: the TrustedOS creates it, oid(0, TI), with the first
--- instance TI of the TA, records it in ta-storages, and gives it to the later instances.  The
--- entry points TA_CreateEntryPoint and TA_OpenSessionEntryPoint are not modeled: the instance is
--- created and the session opened at once.  An RA gets the return code, and the new session
--- after success; it is not given the return origin.  A TA gets the code, the handle, which is
--- TEE_HANDLE_NULL on failure, and the origin.
---
--- Invoking a command.  The source of an idle session sends its request to the destination
--- through the session; a request through the session of another client is not served.  The
--- instance serves one request at a time, see [Internal Core] 2.1.3: the requests of the other
--- sessions wait, as invkTa messages, until it is free, and the next one is chosen
--- nondeterministically.  A finished service succeeds, as a service is a void function: the
--- client gets success, with the origin of the TA for a TA client.  A TA instance that panics
--- while it serves the request answers TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD, with the origin of the TEE for a TA
--- client, see [Internal Core] 4.9.3, and no results: the shared objects of the client are
--- unchanged.  Every waiting or later request to a panicked instance gets TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD
--- too, see [Internal Core] 2.3.3.  The panicked instance is destroyed at once, see [Internal
--- Core] 2.3.3: the TA has no instance any more (it is removed from ta-instances), even while
--- other sessions are still open on it.  The sessions stay until their clients close them; a
--- later TEEC_OpenSession of a single-instance TA creates a new instance.
---
--- Closing a session (TEEC_CloseSession of an RA, [Client API] 4.5.8).  The Session object is
--- removed.  When it was the last session of its instance, the instance is destroyed: the TA has
--- no instance any more; its storage stays, see [Internal Core] 2.2.  This is the rule of
--- gpd.ta.instanceKeepAlive false ([Internal Core] 4.5), the only one the model has: an instance of
--- a multi-instance TA has one session, and a single-instance TA is not kept alive.  A later
--- TEEC_OpenSession of a single-instance TA whose storage exists creates a new instance with that
--- storage.  The entry points TA_CloseSessionEntryPoint and TA_DestroyEntryPoint are not modeled,
--- and the objects that the destroyed instance owned (its handles) are left in the configuration,
--- unreachable.  TEE_CloseTASession of a TA is not modeled.
--- The C call of an RA, teecOpenSession, is in RICH-APP-BEHAVIOR, and teecInvokeCommand in
--- SHARED-MEMORY-BEHAVIOR.

--- @kind state
--- @feature ta-session
omod SESSION is
  pr OBJECT-ID .
  pr SESSION-ID .

  subsort SessionId < Oid .

  sort SessionState .
  op idle : -> SessionState [ctor] .
  op invoking : -> SessionState [ctor] .
  op targetDead : -> SessionState [ctor] .

  class Session | source : Oid , destination : Oid , is-smc : Bool , state : SessionState .
endom

--- @kind behavior
--- @feature ta-session
omod SESSION-BEHAVIOR is
  pr SESSION .
  pr TEE-OS-BEHAVIOR .
  pr TRUST-APP .
  pr SECURE-MONITOR-CALL .
  pr INVOKE-TA-CALL .
  pr HANDLE-AUX .
  pr TEE-MSG .
  pr TEE-CLIENT-FUNC .
  pr TEE-INTERNAL-CLIENT-FUNC .
  pr TEE-CLIENT-VALUE .
  pr RETURN-VALUE .
  pr SHARED-OBJECT .

  op #_ : FuncId -> Value [ctor] .
  op #_ : List{Arg} -> Value [ctor] .

  vars OS RI O TI HI : Oid .
  vars TN TA : AppId .
  vars N M : Nat .
  var MS : Bool .
  var P : Program .
  var SIL : List{Service} .
  var SOL : List{ServiceReturn} .
  var SID : SessionId .
  var CFG : Map{AppId,TaConfig} .
  vars IM ST : Map{AppId,Oid} .
  var SI : Oid .
  var FID : FuncId .
  vars VL RET : List{Arg} .
  var V : Value .
  var ARGS : List{Arg} .
  var RC : ReturnCode .
  var KS : KConfig .
  var TIMEOUTARG : Value .
  var RESTARGS : List{Arg} .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Opening a session: the TrustedOS, for an RA (TEEC_OpenSession)
------------------------------------------------------------

--- teec-open-session: the single-instance TA TN has no instance, so the TrustedOS creates the TA
--- instance oid(N, OS) with the program P of TN and the storage of TN, records them, and opens the
--- session sessionId(N) of the RA RI on it.
  crl [teec-open-session] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, MS) , CFG) , ta-instances : IM ,
                       ta-storages : ST , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : (TN |-> oid(N, OS) , IM) ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , ST) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : RI , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : true , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    < oid(0, oid(N, OS)) : Storage | status : (normal).StorageStatus , files : empty , counter : 0 >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N)))
  if not $hasMapping(IM, TN) /\ not $hasMapping(ST, TN) .

--- teec-open-session-busy: the instance TI of TN already has a session, and TN accepts one
--- session at a time: TEEC_ERROR_BUSY.
  rl [teec-open-session-busy] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, false) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : s M >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | >
    < TI : TrustedApp | >
    smcRet(RI, # errorBusy) .

--- teec-open-session-instance: TN is a multi-instance TA, so the TrustedOS creates the instance
--- oid(N, OS) for the session sessionId(N) of the RA RI.  TN has no storage yet: it is created
--- with this first instance, oid(0, oid(N, OS)), and recorded.
  crl [teec-open-session-instance] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, false, MS) , CFG) ,
                       ta-storages : ST , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-storages : (TN |-> oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , ST) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : RI , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : true , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    < oid(0, oid(N, OS)) : Storage | status : (normal).StorageStatus , files : empty , counter : 0 >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N)))
  if not $hasMapping(ST, TN) .

--- teec-open-session-instance-storage: the same, when TN has the storage SI: the new instance
--- gets SI.
  rl [teec-open-session-instance-storage] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, false, MS) , CFG) ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> SI , ST) , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : RI , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : true , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : SI , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N))) .

--- teec-open-session-shared: TN has the instance TI and accepts several sessions, so the
--- session sessionId(N) of the RA RI is opened on TI.
  rl [teec-open-session-shared] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, true) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) , session-counter : N >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : M >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | session-counter : N + 1 >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : s M >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : RI , destination : TI , is-smc : true , state : idle >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N))) .

--- teec-open-session-storage: the single-instance TA TN has no instance but has the storage SI (its
--- earlier instance was destroyed, see teec-close-session-last), so the TrustedOS creates the
--- instance oid(N, OS) with the program P of TN and the storage SI, records it, and opens the
--- session sessionId(N) of the RA RI on it.
  crl [teec-open-session-storage] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, MS) , CFG) , ta-instances : IM ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> SI , ST) , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : (TN |-> oid(N, OS) , IM) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : RI , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : true , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : SI , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    smcRet(RI, (# success # sessionId(N)))
  if not $hasMapping(IM, TN) .

--- teec-open-session-not-found: no TA has the identifier TN: TEEC_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND.
  crl [teec-open-session-not-found] :
    smcReq(RI, teecOpenSession, # TN)
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-config : CFG >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | >
    smcRet(RI, # errorItemNotFound)
  if not $hasMapping(CFG, TN) .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Closing a session: an RA (TEEC_CloseSession)
------------------------------------------------------------

--- teec-close-session: the session SID of the RA RI is removed; its instance TI has another
--- session, so it stays.
  rl [teec-close-session] :
    smcReq(RI, teecCloseSession, # SID)
    < SID : Session | source : RI , destination : TI , is-smc : true >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : s s M >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : s M >
    smcRet(RI, # success) .

--- teec-close-session-last: the session SID of RI was the last session of its instance TI, which
--- is destroyed: the TA of TI has no instance.
  rl [teec-close-session-last] :
    smcReq(RI, teecCloseSession, # SID)
    < SID : Session | source : RI , destination : TI , is-smc : true >
    < TI : TrustedApp | client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : IM >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : 0 >
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : dropInstance(TI, IM) >
    smcRet(RI, # success) .

  --- dropInstance(TI, IM): IM without the entry of the instance TI.  A multi-instance TA has no
  --- entry, and a single-instance TA whose instance TI has panicked may have a newer instance.
  op dropInstance : Oid Map{AppId,Oid} -> Map{AppId,Oid} .
  eq dropInstance(TI, (TN |-> TI , IM)) = IM .
  eq dropInstance(TI, IM) = IM [owise] .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Opening a session: the TrustedOS, for a TA (openTASession)
------------------------------------------------------------

--- open-ta-session: the single-instance TA TN has no instance, so the TrustedOS creates the TA
--- instance oid(N, OS) with the program P of TN from ta-config and the storage of TN,
--- oid(0, oid(N, OS)) with no files, records them, and opens the session sessionId(N) of the
--- requesting TA O on it.  openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N)) is queued in service-out.
  crl [open-ta-session] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : O ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, MS) , CFG) , ta-instances : IM ,
                       ta-storages : ST , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> oid(N, OS) , IM) ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , ST) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : O , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : false , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    < oid(0, oid(N, OS)) : Storage | status : (normal).StorageStatus , files : empty , counter : 0 >
  if not $hasMapping(IM, TN) /\ not $hasMapping(ST, TN) .

--- open-ta-session-busy: the instance TI of TN already has a session, and TN accepts one session
--- at a time, so the session is not opened: TEE_ERROR_BUSY, [Internal Core] 4.9.1.
  rl [open-ta-session-busy] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, false) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : s M >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionFail(errorBusy)) >
    < TI : TrustedApp | >
  .

--- open-ta-session-instance: TN is a multi-instance TA, so the TrustedOS creates the instance
--- oid(N, OS) for the session sessionId(N) of the requesting TA O.  TN has no storage yet: it is
--- created with this first instance, oid(0, oid(N, OS)), and recorded.
  crl [open-ta-session-instance] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : O ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, false, MS) , CFG) ,
                       ta-storages : ST , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , ST) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : O , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : false , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : oid(0, oid(N, OS)) , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
    < oid(0, oid(N, OS)) : Storage | status : (normal).StorageStatus , files : empty , counter : 0 >
  if not $hasMapping(ST, TN) .

--- open-ta-session-instance-storage: the same, when TN has the storage SI: the new instance gets
--- SI.
  rl [open-ta-session-instance-storage] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : O ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, false, MS) , CFG) ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> SI , ST) , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : O , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : false , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : SI , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
  .

--- open-ta-session-shared: TN has the instance TI and accepts several sessions, so the session
--- sessionId(N) of the requesting TA O is opened on TI.
  rl [open-ta-session-shared] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : O ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, true) , CFG) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> TI , IM) , session-counter : N >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : M >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < TI : TrustedApp | sessions : s M >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : O , destination : TI , is-smc : false , state : idle >
  .

--- open-ta-session-storage: the single-instance TA TN has no instance but has the storage SI, so
--- the TrustedOS creates the instance oid(N, OS) with the program P of TN and the storage SI,
--- records it, and opens the session sessionId(N) of the requesting TA O on it.
  crl [open-ta-session-storage] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       service-request-ta-inst : O ,
                       ta-config : (TN |-> taConfig(P, true, MS) , CFG) , ta-instances : IM ,
                       ta-storages : (TN |-> SI , ST) , session-counter : N >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionSuccess(sessionId(N))) ,
                       ta-instances : (TN |-> oid(N, OS) , IM) ,
                       session-counter : N + 1 >
    < sessionId(N) : Session | source : O , destination : oid(N, OS) , is-smc : false , state : idle >
    < oid(N, OS) : TrustedApp | proc : none , prog : P ,
                                 status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : noCall , counter : 1 ,
                                 storage : SI , os-kernel : OS ,
                                 client-service : none , sessions : 1 >
  if not $hasMapping(IM, TN) .

--- open-ta-session-not-found: no TA has the identifier TN, so the session is not opened:
--- TEE_ERROR_ITEM_NOT_FOUND, [Internal Core] 4.9.1.
  crl [open-ta-session-not-found] :
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : (openTASession(TN) SIL) , service-out : SOL ,
                       ta-config : CFG >
    =>
    < OS : TrustedOS | service-in : SIL , service-out : (SOL openSessionFail(errorItemNotFound)) >
  if not $hasMapping(CFG, TN) .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Opening a session: the TA (TEE_OpenTASession)
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- The 'TEE_OpenTASession' function opens a new session with a Trusted Application.
  --- See page 98 of the G.P. documentation for more details.

  --- open-session-subroutine: the init call of TeeOpenTASession becomes final, and the
  --- TrustedOS is asked to open a session with the TA TA.
  rl [open-session-subroutine] :
    < O : TAKernel | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : init(TeeOpenTASession[# TA TIMEOUTARG RESTARGS]) >
    =>
    < O : TAKernel | api-call : final(TeeOpenTASession[# TA TIMEOUTARG RESTARGS]) >
    reqTrustedOS(openTASession(TA) , O)
  .

  --- open-session-success: the openSessionSuccess(SID) answer of the TrustedOS finishes the
  --- call with success and the handle oid(N, O) of the session SID, which is created, and the
  --- counter advances by one.
  rl [open-session-success] :
    retTrustedOS(openSessionSuccess(SID), O)
    < O : TAKernel | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : final(TeeOpenTASession[ARGS]) , counter : N >
    =>
    < O : TAKernel | api-call : return(TeeOpenTASession[# success # oid(N, O) # originTrustedApp]) ,
                      counter : N + 1 >
    freshSessionHandle(N, O, SID)
  .

  --- open-session-fail: the openSessionFail(RC) answer of the TrustedOS finishes the call with
  --- the code RC, the origin of the TEE, and TEE_HANDLE_NULL as the handle, see [Internal Core]
  --- 4.9.1.  No handle is created.
  rl [open-session-fail] :
    retTrustedOS(openSessionFail(RC), O)
    < O : TAKernel | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : final(TeeOpenTASession[ARGS]) >
    =>
    < O : TAKernel | api-call : return(TeeOpenTASession[# RC # null # originTee]) >
  .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Invoking a command: an RA (TEEC_InvokeCommand)
------------------------------------------------------------

--- handle-smc-request: the SMC request of the RA RI in its idle session SID is sent by the
--- session to its destination TI as invkTa (App D.3), and a command is pending in SID.  A request
--- through the session of another client is not served.
  rl [handle-smc-request] :
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, VL)
    < SID : Session | source : RI , destination : TI , is-smc : true , state : idle >
    =>
    < SID : Session | state : invoking >
    (msg invkTa[FID VL] from SID to TI) .

--- handle-smc-request-target-dead: the destination of the session SID has panicked, so a request
--- of the RA RI in it gets TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD at once.
  rl [handle-smc-request-target-dead] :
    smcReq(RI, SID, FID, VL)
    < SID : Session | source : RI , is-smc : true , state : targetDead >
    =>
    < SID : Session | >
    smcRet(RI, # errorTargetDead) .

--- handle-smc-request-finish: the response invkTaRet of the destination TI to the session SID is
--- sent to the RA RI as an SMC response, with the return code success; SID is idle again.
  rl [handle-smc-request-finish] :
    (msg invkTaRet[RET] from TI to SID)
    < SID : Session | source : RI , destination : TI , is-smc : true , state : invoking >
    =>
    < SID : Session | state : idle >
    smcRet(RI, (# success RET)) .

--- return-smc-request-panic: a TA instance that panics while it serves the request of the session
--- SID of the RA RI returns TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD to RI (Fig 21).  The TA has no client-service
--- afterwards, the session is targetDead, and the instance is destroyed: the TA has no instance
--- in ta-instances any more.
  rl [return-smc-request-panic] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic , client-service : {SID , FID} >
    < SID : Session | source : RI , is-smc : true , state : invoking >
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : IM >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | client-service : none >
    < SID : Session | state : targetDead >
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : dropInstance(TI, IM) >
    smcRet(RI, # errorTargetDead) .

--- return-smc-request-dead: a request of the session SID of the RA RI to a TA instance that has
--- panicked, waiting or sent after the panic, is not served: TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD, and the
--- session is targetDead.
  rl [return-smc-request-dead] :
    (msg invkTa[FID VL] from SID to TI)
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic >
    < SID : Session | source : RI , is-smc : true , state : invoking >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | >
    < SID : Session | state : targetDead >
    smcRet(RI, # errorTargetDead) .

------------------------------------------------------------
--- Invoking a command: a TA (TEE_InvokeTACommand)
------------------------------------------------------------

  --- The 'TEE_InvokeTACommand' function invokes a command within a session opened between the
  --- client Trusted Application instance and a destination Trusted Application instance.
  --- See page 101 of the G.P. documentation for more details.

  --- copyIn and copyOut (SHARED-OBJECT): the shared objects of the client, given by the language.

  --- invoke-ta-command-request: the init call of TeeInvokeTACommand becomes final, and the idle
  --- session SID that the handle HI names sends invkTa to its destination TI, with the values
  --- of the arguments VL; a command is pending in SID.  A request through the session of another
  --- client is not served.
  rl [invoke-ta-command-request] :
    < O : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus ,
                        api-call : init(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HI # FID VL]) ,
                        proc : KS >
    < HI : TaSessionHandle | session : SID >
    < SID : Session | source : O , destination : TI , is-smc : false , state : idle >
    =>
    < O : TrustedApp | api-call : final(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HI # FID VL]) >
    < HI : TaSessionHandle | >
    < SID : Session | state : invoking >
    (msg invkTa[FID copyIn(VL, KS)] from SID to TI)
  .

  --- invoke-ta-command-target-dead: the destination of the session SID has panicked, so the call
  --- returns TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD with the origin of the TEE at once.
  rl [invoke-ta-command-target-dead] :
    < O : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus ,
                        api-call : init(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HI # FID VL]) >
    < HI : TaSessionHandle | session : SID >
    < SID : Session | source : O , is-smc : false , state : targetDead >
    =>
    < O : TrustedApp | api-call : return(TeeInvokeTACommand[# errorTargetDead # originTee]) >
    < HI : TaSessionHandle | >
    < SID : Session | >
  .

  --- invoke-ta-command-finish: the response invkTaRet of the destination TI to the session SID of
  --- the TA O: the results RET are copied back to the shared objects of O, TeeInvokeTACommand
  --- returns success with the origin of the TA, and SID is idle again.
  rl [invoke-ta-command-finish] :
    (msg invkTaRet[RET] from TI to SID)
    < SID : Session | source : O , destination : TI , is-smc : false , state : invoking >
    < O : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus ,
                        api-call : final(TeeInvokeTACommand[# HI # FID VL]) ,
                        proc : KS >
    =>
    < SID : Session | state : idle >
    < O : TrustedApp | api-call : return(TeeInvokeTACommand[# success # originTrustedApp]) ,
                        proc : copyOut(VL, RET, KS) >
  .

  --- return-session-request-panic: a TA instance that panics while it serves the request of the
  --- session SID of the TA O returns TeeInvokeTACommand of O with TEE_ERROR_TARGET_DEAD and the
  --- origin of the TEE, see [Internal Core] 4.9.3; the shared objects of O are unchanged.  The
  --- instance is destroyed as in return-smc-request-panic.
  rl [return-session-request-panic] :
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic , client-service : {SID , FID} >
    < SID : Session | source : O , is-smc : false , state : invoking >
    < O : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : final(TeeInvokeTACommand[ARGS]) >
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : IM >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | client-service : none >
    < SID : Session | state : targetDead >
    < O : TrustedApp | api-call : return(TeeInvokeTACommand[# errorTargetDead # originTee]) >
    < OS : TrustedOS | ta-instances : dropInstance(TI, IM) > .

  --- return-session-request-dead: the same for a request of the session SID of the TA O to a
  --- panicked instance, waiting or sent after the panic.
  rl [return-session-request-dead] :
    (msg invkTa[FID VL] from SID to TI)
    < TI : TrustedApp | status : panic >
    < SID : Session | source : O , is-smc : false , state : invoking >
    < O : TrustedApp | status : (normal).AppStatus , api-call : final(TeeInvokeTACommand[ARGS]) >
    =>
    < TI : TrustedApp | >
    < SID : Session | state : targetDead >
    < O : TrustedApp | api-call : return(TeeInvokeTACommand[# errorTargetDead # originTee]) > .
endom
